ItemTitle: Is the static ObjectMapper instance thread-safe and appropriately configured to handle various MCP schema types without polluting global state?
Answer:
ChecklistItemAnswer[finalAnswer=The static ObjectMapper instance in McpToolUtils is not configured to be thread-safe or to handle MCP schema types. It is created without configuration, while a different bean (mcpServerObjectMapper) is configured via auto-configuration., analysis=The McpServerObjectMapperAutoConfiguration provides configuration for a different ObjectMapper bean (mcpServerObjectMapper) with proper deserialization settings and module registration. However, the static OBJECT_MAPPER instance in McpToolUtils is created without any configuration and is not shown to be thread-safe or properly configured for MCP schema types. The checklist requires the static instance to be both thread-safe and appropriately configured, but no such configuration is present in the code., evidence=[EvidenceItem[file=mcp/common/src/main/java/org/springframework/ai/mcp/McpToolUtils.java, lines=37-38, reason=The code declares a static final ObjectMapper OBJECT_MAPPER = new ObjectMapper(); which creates a single instance of ObjectMapper. However, this instance is not configured with any of the configuration methods (e.g., setDefaultTypeHandling, registerModules) that would make it thread-safe or handle MCP schema types appropriately.], EvidenceItem[file=mcp/common/src/main/java/org/springframework/ai/mcp/McpToolUtils.java, lines=74-89, reason=The parseContentList method uses OBJECT_MAPPER.readTree() to deserialize JSON nodes. While the McpServerObjectMapperAutoConfiguration shows configuration for a different ObjectMapper bean, there is no evidence that the static OBJECT_MAPPER instance in McpToolUtils is configured or that it is thread-safe.]]]
